{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791100577,"nonce":"liCIkAbUXdPWRm5LziSOL/mt7NM=","title":"Layout animation: FLIP for bounds changes","message":"User direction (2026-10-04): prioritise layout animations, which Blinc does with FLIP (blinc_layout visual_animation: layout settles at once, the renderer draws the element offset from its laid-out bounds, the offset springs back to zero; content clipped to the animated bounds rather than scaled; offsets carried to children). In ashui, in Haxe: after a layout pass, an element marked to animate its bounds compares them with the last; position as a transform from the inverse delta springing to identity, size as clip-path inset easing to the full box (both render-only, no relayout). Needed by Accordion, Collapsible, the tabs indicator, toasts, list reorder.","files":null}]}